      "id": "group-303-305",
      "section": "Social Studies",
      "questionStart": 303,
      "questionEnd": 305,
      "rangeLabel": "Questions 303–305",
      "contextType": "map",
      "marker": "Questions 303 through 305.",
      "context": "Beginning at the end of the 15th century, many European countries\nbegan exploring and conquering territories in the New World. Driven by\nthe desire for increased economic wealth, access to natural resources,\nand the wish to spread Christianity to new parts of the world, many\nEuropean nations formed permanent settlements in the New World.\nThe following map shows the New World during this period and labels\nthe European countries that controlled each territory at that time.",
