          "number": 428,
          "text": "428. A tariff is a special tax that is imposed on imported goods and\n     services to restrict trade and increase the price of imported goods\n     and services. The United States occasionally imposes tariffs in an\n     attempt to persuade Americans to buy American-made goods and\n     services.\n     According to the given information, which of the following is an\n     example of a tariff?\n     (A) Congress imposes a tax on beer that is manufactured in\n       California but sold in New York.\n     (B) Congress increases the price of all gasoline to fund clean energy\n       research.\n     (C) Congress imposes a tax on imported Japanese cars in order to\n       protect domestic car sales.\n     (D) Congress creates a flat-tax rate for all income levels.\n\nUse the following graph and information for",
