      "questions": [
        {
          "number": 436,
          "text": "436. Based on the graph, in what year will the world population reach 8\n     billion people?\n     (A) 2015\n     (B) 2018\n\n   (C) 2022\n   (D) 2028",
          "sourcePage": 175
        },
        {
          "number": 437,
          "text": "437. Based on the tables, which country’s population is expected to\n   grow by the biggest percentage by 2050?\n   (A) China\n   (B) India\n   (C) Nigeria\n   (D) United States",
          "sourcePage": 175
        },
        {
          "number": 438,
          "text": "438. Based on the graph, which of the following is a true statement\n   regarding the predicted global population growth?\n   (A) Most of the population growth is expected to come from less\n     developed countries.\n   (B) Most of the population growth is expected to come from more\n     developed countries.\n   (C) Both developed and less developed countries contribute equally\n     to the predicted population growth.\n   (D) The global population is expected to remain relatively steady\n     until 2050.",
          "sourcePage": 176
        },
        {
          "number": 439,
          "text": "439. Based on the given information, which of the following is a factual\n   statement?\n   (A) China’s population is expected to rise steadily by 2050.\n   (B) All of the top 10 most populous countries in 2013 will still be in\n     the top 10 most populous countries in 2050.\n   (C) The world population appears to be doubling in size every 40 to\n     60 years.\n   (D) Russia’s population will fall by 2050.",
          "sourcePage": 176
        },
        {
          "number": 440,
          "text": "440. Based on the given information, which of the following is an\n    opinion rather than a factual statement?\n\n     (A) China’s population is expected to fall slightly by 2050.\n     (B) Nigeria should encourage birth control measures to prevent its\n       population from growing too quickly.\n     (C) The United States population is expected to grow by less than\n       30% by 2050.\n     (D) India is expected to become the most populous country in the\n       world by 2050.",
          "sourcePage": 176
        }
      ]
