          "number": 838,
          "text": "838. Why does the passage refer to Edward K. Wehling, Jr. as “Young\n   Wehling” and describe him as “a mere stripling,” even though he is\n   56 years old?\n   (A) You are only as young as you feel.\n   (B) The average age of the population is 129.\n   (C) He is in exceptionally good health.\n   (D) He is actually only 26 years old.",
